      {
        "id": 140515,
        "name": "Arcanist Lupus",
        "username": "Arcanist_Lupus",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/arcanist_lupus/{size}/2169_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-04-20T05:26:35.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Greywind\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/greywind/48/2006_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Greywind:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>It isn't being destroyed, nor is it going into the Baron's play area. It is going under the character card and having no effect upon the game, at least until he flips.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Not quite correct, I think.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Whenever a Villain Target enters play, put it under this card and play the top card of the Villain deck. Cards under this card have no game text, are indestructible, and are not considered in play.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>This says to me that the card does enter Blade's play area. &nbsp;It then stays in the Baron's play area, but loses all text (because it's under his card). &nbsp;Therefore, the card is being played (since that's how it enters play, which is what causes it to be moved under the Blade), and should destroy Twisting Back Alleys.</p>",
